{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Does Computer Architecture Mean?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about Computer Architecture."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.   Make the information system design report, based on the selection of both hardware and software tools required for the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.     Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adjectives As\u2026 As, Er, and More"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you need to compare the different characteristics of something, you can use <span class=\"strong\">comparatives</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  There are different ways to compare characteristics of objects. This learning point helps you understand three of them. The first one is by adding <span class=\"strong\">\u2013er</span> to short adjectives. The second form is by using the structure <span class=\"strong\">more\u2026than</span> with long adjectives. The last one is by using <span class=\"strong\">as\u2026as</span> to state that there is some equality between the two objects you compare.<br/><br/>  The following chart exemplifies the appropriate use of these three cases of comparison."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1.   \u2013er <br/> (short adjectives)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">adjective + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">er </span> + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">than</span> + complement<br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">This program runs fast<span class=\\\"strong\\\">er than</span> the default application.</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">2. more\u2026than<br/> (long adjectives)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">more</span> + adjective + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">than</span> + complement<br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">The previous design is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">more interesting than </span> the new one.</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">3. as\u2026as<br/> (any adjective)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">as</span> + adjective + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">as</span> + complement<br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">In computer architecture, logic design is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">as fundamental as  </span> microarchitecture design.</span></div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you can see computer architecture is as important as software architecture and, for some, it is even considered more important."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This process can be more complex than other ones since it involves microarchitecture design, logic design, instruction set architecture design, and implementation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Though implementation isn't part of the computer architecture field at all, it is as essential as the previous ones."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Timeline: the Evolution of Personal Computers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The personal computer, or PC, is one of the greatest inventions of the XX century. Thanks to this technological tool, we simplify all of our activities, from daily tasks to the most complex processes in our jobs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at the following timeline to see the progress of personal computers through the years:"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "architecture "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the internal design of hardware and software in a computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Computer architecture refers to some methods and rules that define computer systems, in terms of their functions, organization, and implementation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "method "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a procedure to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Computer architecture refers to some methods and rules that define computer systems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pipeline processor "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sequence of processed data in which the output of one factor is the input of the following factor"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It works through pipeline processors, which consist of linear and sequential segments that perform specific tasks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "microarchitecture "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the organization of the computer; for instance, the implementation of processors"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It involves microarchitecture design, logic design, instruction set architecture design and implementation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "circuit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an electronic path that communicates one point with another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It implies to check the transistors design to create physical circuits and to validate the final design."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "validate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to confirm something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What do you mean by validating the final design?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research about the main steps or components of computer architecture."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a diagram resenting each part and how they are connected between them"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your diagram to a partner, explain and answer any questions about the topic"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about computer architecture"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a diagram to explain"}, {"type": "text", "con